@startuml
title The same long, executed on Hyperliquid and on GMX V2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam SequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam SequenceParticipantBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam SequenceBoxBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam SequenceBoxBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #4A78B5

actor Trader

box "Hyperliquid" #F7FAFF
  participant "HyperBFT\n+ HyperCore" as HL
  participant "Order book" as OB
  participant "Resting maker" as MK
end box

box "GMX V2" #F7FAFF
  participant "Order contract" as GC
  participant "Keeper" as KP
  participant "GM pool (LPs)" as LP
end box

== Hyperliquid: a counterparty has to exist ==
Trader -> HL : signed IOC buy, size S, limit P
HL -> OB : committed, sorted into the GTC/IOC class
OB -> MK : match at price-time priority
note over OB, MK
  Price is whatever the resting
  orders say. Depth beyond P
  leaves the order unfilled.
end note
MK --> Trader : fill at the maker's price
OB --> Trader : remainder cancelled (IOC)

== GMX V2: the pool is always the counterparty ==
Trader -> GC : create order request (onchain)
note right of GC
  Nothing has executed yet.
  The request states intent only.
end note
KP -> KP : fetch a signed Chainlink\nData Streams price
KP -> GC : execute with that price
GC -> LP : open the position against the pool
note over GC, LP
  Entry uses the oracle maxPrice for a long.
  No price impact at entry; impact applies
  when the position is closed or decreased.
  Execution is not guaranteed.
end note
LP --> Trader : position opened at the oracle price
@enduml
